<p> Wages and Salaries   3,751  3,755  3,755  3,714  3,710  3,682</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   690    693    693    683    683    680</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,318  1,322  1,324  1,299  1,298  1,285</p>
<p> -Government		653    648    647    647    647    647</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    534    533    533    532    532    531</p>
<p> -Farm			 47     48     47     50     49     51</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  487    485    485    483    483    480</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected January personal income to rise 0.1 percent and spending to be up 0.6 percent.  </p>
<p>January's personal income was boosted by cost-of-living adjustments to several federal transfer payment programs, changes to the Earned Income Credit Program, and pay raises for federal, civilian and military personnel, the department said.</p>
<p>The increase was limited, though, by program changes that affected personal contributions for social insurance and by lump sum social security benefits payments that had raised December personal income.</p>
<p>Without these special factors, the department said personal income rose $5.3 billion, or less than 0.1 percent, in January.</p>
